[["Map",1,2,68,69],"blog",["Map",3,4,32,33],"test",{"id":3,"data":5,"body":12,"filePath":13,"digest":14,"rendered":15},{"title":6,"description":7,"pubDate":8,"tags":9,"featured":11},"My Test Post","This is a test of the upload feature",["Date","2026-08-02T00:00:00.000Z"],[3,10],"demo",false,"# My Test Post\n\nThis is the content of my test post.\n\n- List item 1\n- List item 2\n\n```javascript\nconst code = \"example\"\n```\n\n## Test Markdown","src/content/blog/test.md","af18e7e13c3757ef",{"html":16,"metadata":17},"\u003Ch1 id=\"my-test-post\">My Test Post\u003C/h1>\n\u003Cp>This is the content of my test post.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>List item 1\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>List item 2\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cpre class=\"astro-code astro-code-themes vitesse-light vitesse-dark\" style=\"background-color:#ffffff;--shiki-dark-bg:#121212;color:#393a34;--shiki-dark:#dbd7caee; overflow-x: auto;\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"javascript\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#AB5959;--shiki-dark:#CB7676\">const\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#B07D48;--shiki-dark:#BD976A\"> code\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#999999;--shiki-dark:#666666\"> =\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#B5695977;--shiki-dark:#C98A7D77\"> \"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#B56959;--shiki-dark:#C98A7D\">example\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#B5695977;--shiki-dark:#C98A7D77\">\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"test-markdown\">Test Markdown\u003C/h2>",{"headings":18,"localImagePaths":26,"remoteImagePaths":27,"frontmatter":28,"imagePaths":31},[19,22],{"depth":20,"slug":21,"text":6},1,"my-test-post",{"depth":23,"slug":24,"text":25},2,"test-markdown","Test Markdown",[],[],{"title":6,"description":7,"pubDate":29,"tags":30},["Date","2026-08-02T00:00:00.000Z"],[3,10],[],"test-copy",{"id":32,"data":34,"body":43,"filePath":44,"digest":45,"rendered":46},{"title":35,"description":36,"pubDate":37,"tags":38,"featured":42},"Optimizing 3D Assets with GLTF Instancing in Three.js","How we achieved sub-second load times by instancing rendering calls for complex web models.",["Date","2026-02-15T00:00:00.000Z"],[39,40,41],"Three.js","WebGL","Performance",true,"Rendering thousands of duplicate geometries in WebGL can destroy frame rates if managed incorrectly. \n\n## The Problem\n\nTraditional draw calls incur high CPU overhead when rendering repeated 3D objects like trees, rocks, or sci-fi building blocks.\n\n```ts\n// ❌ Avoid this: 1000 individual draw calls\nmodels.forEach((model) => {\n  scene.add(model.clone());\n});\n\nThe Solution: Instancing\n\nBy utilizing GPU instanced meshes, we pass one set of geometry and material data once, then supply transformation matrices per instance.\nTypeScript\n\n// ✅ Efficient: 1 draw call for all instances\nconst instancedMesh = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geometry, material, 1000);\n```\n---\ntitle: \"Optimizing 3D Assets with GLTF Instancing in Three.js\"\ndescription: \"How we achieved sub-second load times by instancing rendering calls for complex web models.\"\npubDate: 2026-02-15\ntags: [\"Three.js\", \"WebGL\", \"Performance\"]\nfeatured: true\n---\n\nRendering thousands of duplicate geometries in WebGL can destroy frame rates if managed incorrectly. \n\n## The Problem\n\nTraditional draw calls incur high CPU overhead when rendering repeated 3D objects like trees, rocks, or sci-fi building blocks.\n\n```ts\n// ❌ Avoid this: 1000 individual draw calls\nmodels.forEach((model) => {\n  scene.add(model.clone());\n});\n\nThe Solution: Instancing\n\nBy utilizing GPU instanced meshes, we pass one set of geometry and material data once, then supply transformation matrices per instance.\nTypeScript\n\n// ✅ Efficient: 1 draw call for all instances\nconst instancedMesh = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geometry, material, 1000);\n```\n---\ntitle: \"Optimizing 3D Assets with GLTF Instancing in Three.js\"\ndescription: \"How we achieved sub-second load times by instancing rendering calls for complex web models.\"\npubDate: 2026-02-15\ntags: [\"Three.js\", \"WebGL\", \"Performance\"]\nfeatured: true\n---\n\nRendering thousands of duplicate geometries in WebGL can destroy frame rates if managed incorrectly. \n\n## The Problem\n\nTraditional draw calls incur high CPU overhead when rendering repeated 3D objects like trees, rocks, or sci-fi building blocks.\n\n```ts\n// ❌ Avoid this: 1000 individual draw calls\nmodels.forEach((model) => {\n  scene.add(model.clone());\n});\n\nThe Solution: Instancing\n\nBy utilizing GPU instanced meshes, we pass one set of geometry and material data once, then supply transformation matrices per instance.\nTypeScript\n\n// ✅ Efficient: 1 draw call for all instances\nconst instancedMesh = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geometry, material, 1000);\n```","src/content/blog/test copy.md","93671656a498d518",{"html":47,"metadata":48},"\u003Cp>Rendering thousands of duplicate geometries in WebGL can destroy frame rates if managed incorrectly.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"the-problem\">The Problem\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Traditional draw calls incur high CPU overhead when rendering repeated 3D objects like trees, rocks, or sci-fi building blocks.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"astro-code astro-code-themes vitesse-light vitesse-dark\" style=\"background-color:#ffffff;--shiki-dark-bg:#121212;color:#393a34;--shiki-dark:#dbd7caee; overflow-x: auto;\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"ts\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#A0ADA0;--shiki-dark:#758575DD\">// ❌ Avoid this: 1000 individual draw calls\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#B07D48;--shiki-dark:#BD976A\">models\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#999999;--shiki-dark:#666666\">.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#59873A;--shiki-dark:#80A665\">forEach\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#999999;--shiki-dark:#666666\">((\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#B07D48;--shiki-dark:#BD976A\">model\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"col